Update: This doesn't work, it's probably not a kenel issue. The radio was working on lineageOS19, and it stopped working on more recent versions.
The [real FM radio app](https://github.com/vladislav805/RFM-Radio) is made for older versions of android, it won't even run on android 14 and 15, I updated the sdk, but it doesn't work anyways.
What we want is to make the [LineageOS radio app work](https://www.apkmirror.com/apk/lineageos/fm-radio-10/fm-radio-10-13-release/fm-radio-13-android-apk-download/) Right now trying to install that app on android 14 gives me:
```
05-01 17:10:57.860 W PackageManager: com.android.server.pm.ReconcileFailure: Reconcile failed: Package com.caf.fmradio requires unavailable shared library qcom.fmradio; failing!
...
05-01 17:10:57.875 D PackageInstallerSession: Marking session 562478839 as failed: INSTALL_FAILED_MISSING_SHARED_LIBRARY: Reconciliation failed...: Reconcile failed: Package com.caf.fmradio requires unavailable shared library qcom.fmradio; failing!
```
Info from main developers on radio support:
> at this point I've neglected [radio] so much that I don't remember if los even ships the hal
and
> [we] should be looking at qcom's fm and bluetooth hals
> the fm library is prebuilt, not OSS, [the problem is with out hal]

As adding these options didn't solve the problem, it's likely not (just?) a kernel issue, so I'm archiving this

Linux kernel
============

This file was moved to Documentation/admin-guide/README.rst

Please notice that there are several guides for kernel developers and users.
These guides can be rendered in a number of formats, like HTML and PDF.

In order to build the documentation, use ``make htmldocs`` or
``make pdfdocs``.

There are various text files in the Documentation/ subdirectory,
several of them using the Restructured Text markup notation.
See Documentation/00-INDEX for a list of what is contained in each file.

Please read the Documentation/process/changes.rst file, as it contains the
requirements for building and running the kernel, and information about
the problems which may result by upgrading your kernel.
